#
# Disarm the host's hardware watchdog at shutdown: watchdogd disarms the timer only when asked to
# stop, and one left armed through a halt would reset the appliance after somebody asked it to power
# off - scripts/xgs/watchdog.sh.
#
# After the kernel follower's rebuild (20-octep, and os-kernelfollow's 21-kernelfollow, each up to ten
# minutes on the reboot that brings a new kernel) and after the coprocessor's watch (22-xgs-feeder),
# before 80-freebsd takes the services and the network down. Until 2026-11-06 this was 05, first of
# all: both watchdogs were off for the whole rebuild, so a coprocessor reset in it - which an XGS
# 3300's host does not come back from - or a host that stopped left the appliance hung until somebody
# pulled the power, instead of reset some two minutes later.
SCRIPT=/usr/local/opnsense/scripts/xgs/watchdog.sh
[ -f "${SCRIPT}" ] || exit 0
/bin/sh "${SCRIPT}" stop > /dev/null 2>&1
exit 0
